  "title": "Erdős Problem #690",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $d_k(p)$ be the density of those integers whose $k$th smallest prime factor is $p$ (i.e. if $p_1<p_2<\\cdots$ are the primes dividing $n$ then $p_k=p$).\nFor fixed $k\\geq 1$ is $d_k(p)$ unimodular in $p$? That is, it first increases in $p$ until its maximum then decreases.",
